---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Community — Nexus Wave Technologies" description="Nexus Community: a calm, accessible home for people, ideas and future participation.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-shell">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Nexus Community</p>
        <h1>People, ideas and useful connections.</h1>
        <p class="lead">The community area is being kept simple for now. Public discussion and posting are intentionally paused while the next community model is designed.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="/posts">Read Nexus Posts</a>
          <a class="button" href="/join-team">Join the Team</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Current status</p>
        <h2>Community chat is disabled for now.</h2>
        <p class="muted">Private chat, friend-to-chat flows and community messaging are not exposed from the public website at this stage.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="community-pillars">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Community scope</p><h2 id="community-pillars">A cleaner structure for what comes next.</h2></div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-4">
        <article class="card community-pillar"><p class="eyebrow">01</p><h3>Posts</h3><p class="muted">The current public content layer for product updates, accessibility notes, guides and community highlights.</p><a class="button" href="/posts">Explore Posts</a></article>
        <article class="card community-pillar"><p class="eyebrow">02</p><h3>People</h3><p class="muted">Future member discovery will focus on names and safe public information only, without exposing private account data.</p></article>
        <article class="card community-pillar disabled-feature"><p class="eyebrow">03</p><h3>Chat</h3><p class="muted">Private messaging is paused. A future version will use a clear mutual-friend rule before any conversation can begin.</p><button class="button" type="button" disabled>Coming later</button></article>
        <article class="card community-pillar"><p class="eyebrow">04</p><h3>Contribute</h3><p class="muted">People can still contribute through the team application process, accessibility work, content and approved initiatives.</p><a class="button" href="/join-team">Join Team</a></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface-soft" aria-labelledby="community-guidelines">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy first</p>
        <h2>Keep public community information minimal.</h2>
        <p class="muted">Public community surfaces should show only the information needed for the experience. Personal email addresses, phone numbers and private account details do not belong in public lists.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Safety</p>
        <h2>Reporting stays available.</h2>
        <p class="muted">The future community design can include profile-level reporting without requiring friendship or chat access.</p>
        <a class="button" href="/women-safety">Open Women Safety Center</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Why this layout</p><h2>Community now behaves like the other website sections.</h2></div></div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card"><h3>Clear</h3><p class="muted">One main purpose per section, with fewer unfinished controls.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Accessible</h3><p class="muted">Semantic headings, readable blocks and straightforward navigation.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Ready to expand</h3><p class="muted">Chat and richer member features can be added later without redesigning the whole public website.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>